# Suspicious DNS Server Change on Windows Endpoint  (FrostArmada / APT28)
# Source rule: ../sigma/windows_suspicious_dns_server_change.yml
# Write-up:    https://www.sohankanna.com/research/frostarmada-how-apt28-turned-old-home-routers-into-a-microsoft-365-interception-network
#
# Requires: Sysmon + Splunk Add-on for Sysmon. Registry value-set = Event ID 13.
#   Sysmon config must include RegistryEvent (Set) for Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces.
# TUNE: the regex in `where` keeps only changes to a non-corporate resolver.

sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=13
    TargetObject="*\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters\\Interfaces\\*"
    (TargetObject="*NameServer" OR TargetObject="*DhcpNameServer")
| where NOT match(Details, "^(10\.|172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.|192\.168\.)")   ``` TUNE: add your ISP/corp resolver IPs ```
| table _time, host, user, Image, TargetObject, Details
| sort - _time
